  "scope": "Large pages in a process's page table (a VmSpace cursor that locks at a large page's level, CursorMut::map_huge, the user page table's items restoring and unmapping a 2 MiB run, Segment::from_raw_unsized) and each CPU's number written to IA32_TSC_AUX at its start. Existing items, kernel mappings, allocation and metadata unchanged. Work item 1.2 (architecture/moruna-os-system.md, section 1B): ACPI S5 after QEMU's test exit device in arch::power::try_poweroff, and a deadline of 2^33 TSC counts on the PIT calibration waits of the TSC and of the APIC timer, each with its fatal line and a power-off; their arithmetic in the two added files, which Moruna's host tests compile. The same deadline on the boot processor's wait for the other CPUs to start (boot/smp.rs, reached through arch::boot_wait), with its fatal line and a power-off. Work item 1.8 (section 1F): Hyper-V or KVM found and named on the console, the TSC's rate from Hyper-V's MSR after kvmclock and CPUID leaf 0x15 and the APIC timer's from Hyper-V's, the PIT looked for before use, the PIC set up only where it answers its probe, and on Hyper-V the guest OS ID and the hypercall page (one frame, mapped read and execute in kernel mode only); hvdef added as a dependency for the x86 kernel target; the decisions in two added files, which Moruna's host tests compile.",
